      "get": {
        "operationId": "health",
        "summary": " Health",
        "parameters": [],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "OK"
          }
        },
        "description": "Answer 200 only when the app serves *and* the configured database answers.\n\nA bare liveness probe would also return 200 when ``DB_*`` in the server\n``.env`` has drifted, which is precisely the failure a deployment health\ncheck exists to catch. Details of a failed probe go to the server log only:\nthe response body is a constant, so a driver error quoting the database\nuser or host cannot reach a public caller or a CI log."
      }
    },
